With this applied in ~/lab/default.jj, rewrite the list in
~/lab/mail.jj:

    ~/lab/default.jj/libexec/mail/rethread.py maildir/cur   # the plan
    ~/lab/default.jj/libexec/mail/rethread.py --apply maildir/cur |
        while read -r id; do notmuch reindex "${id}"; done
    jj commit -m "mail: Thread each revision under its first version"

Testing: on a copy of the list, a dry run finds every revision
through its Link line, plus the unversioned first posting of the
lab-mail jail series, which EXTRA_LINKS names. --apply then rewrites
117 files, and
a second --apply changes nothing. The diff against the original
touches only In-Reply-To and References lines. A fresh notmuch
database on the copy shows 99 threads where there were 142. Each
series is one tree under its first version: signoz v1 to v10 is one
42-message thread, and "notmuch: Tag superseded series and hide them"
holds v2, both v3s, and v4.


